<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry, Count of Portugal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1066–1112</span> · Also known as Henry of Burgundy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry, Count of Portugal, was a Burgundian noble who fought for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a> of León against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a>. Around 1096 he married Alfonso's daughter Teresa and received the County of Portugal, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coimbra">Coimbra</a>. He governed it until his death in 1112, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-portugal">Afonso Henriques</a> became the first King of Portugal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-count-of-portugal.jpg" alt="Henry, Count of Portugal" width="277" height="498" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henry,_Count_of_Portugal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
